; worldnosave.eval — saving inside a random encounter is REFUSED.
;
; The save is an `expect-refuse` line: it must be refused, so the script PASSES
; when the guard holds (it was written to FAIL before the runner could say a
; refusal was the point - code-review C442). tools/WorldTest.py also reads the
; LOG, and checks the save file was not created either.
;
; What is being guarded: an encounter level exists only in memory, so a save
; naming it would reload into a level that no longer exists and cannot be
; rebuilt. Refusing is recoverable; writing it is not. This is NOT an answer to
; the parked question of what a mid-encounter save should DO
; (docs/world-map.md) — it is the guard that stops the absence of an answer
; becoming a corrupt file.
logecho on
reset
seed 4
leave
worldpos 6 6
encounter
expect-refuse save encountertrip
